      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "For any source classical field and fixed real matrix, choose the existing spatial derivative as the outer witness at each point. The translated right-hand condition is precisely equation (1.1), and its equivalent left-hand condition is equation (1.8) with f(v)=Av. Applying this at every relevant point yields the selected conservation-law identification."
    },
    "source_implies_translation": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "The source identifies the two differential expressions for the fixed linear flux. Under the translated spatial derivative hypothesis, differentiation of the finite constant linear combination gives (Aq)_x=Aq_x. If the time derivative exists, both conditions therefore express the same equation; if it does not, both existential conditions are false. Derivative uniqueness reconciles their independent witnesses. The additional zero-dimensional case is immediate from the unique empty vector and contributes no substantive extension."
